WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:01.010
You Win!

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.470
Police Superintendent's
TOURNAMENT

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.810
Metropolitan Police
JUDO

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:15.320
Good luck, Special Vehicles.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.740
You can do it!

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.740
I don't believe this!

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:24.870
We have to fight that gorilla
on our day off!

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.870
Every police unit is
required to attend.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.750
And since Division 1 is on duty,
it's up to us.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.630
Just accept it.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.970
Round one. Team Red:
Special Vehicles.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.140
Team White: Division 4,
Mobile B team.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:44.930
Bow.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.560
Go for it, guys!

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.600
Team Red:
Starting player, Shinshi.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.810
Team white,
Saito is starting.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:55.860
It's hopeless.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.230
You may be right.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:57.990
Begin!

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.160
I give him three seconds.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.370
Next, Shinohara!

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:14.290
Another white belt?
Don't they have anyone good?

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.500
Saito, go easy on the boy.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.630
They're helpless when
they're out of their Labors.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:20.840
Begin!

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.560
Yeah! Full point!

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:30.980
That was careless.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:35.360
If you succeed, a surprise move
can take out an opponent.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.030
But if you blow it,
you'll only make them madder.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:40.610
Begin!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.450
- Choke hold!
- Enough! Full point!

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.870
Next: Ota.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.330
Ota...

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:59.590
Stop whining!
I'll take all five of them!

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.760
Captain Goto.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.690
Maybe the wind is changing.
He's got a black belt after all.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:17.400
Big deal. My brother has
a whole closet full of them.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.110
Begin!

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.950
What's wrong, Saito?
Hurry up!

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.450
Try not to kill him!

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:37.750
Come at me.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.130
Hello, Goto here.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.050
Oh, Shinobu!
How are you?

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.980
Really? Where?

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.600
Roger. Over and out.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.820
I realize we're in a match,

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.950
but Division 1 has
called for backup.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.580
I request permission to
leave for the crime scene.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:16.170
Of course. You must do your duty.
Proceed immediately.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:21.590
Special Vehicles, Second Section,
Division 2, heading out.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:32.510
Goto.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.520
What happened to your Labor?

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:40.310
Machine 2: Move out as soon
as you take position in back.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:41.400
Roger.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.650
What's the situation?

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:51.370
Terrible. A Shinohara Boxer
is cornered in the public bath.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.830
The perpetrator's girlfriend
dumped him, so he got drunk.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.790
That's not so bad.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.790
It's worse.
A customer tried to escape...

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:01.790
A hostage?

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.590
Captain, Ota is...

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:04.510
What's wrong?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.180
He sprained his ankle?

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:14.930
From the match. And Asuma's
throat is hurt, so he can't talk.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:18.190
Perfect timing.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.610
Machine 1 has no commander,
and machine 2 has no pilot.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.150
What should we do?

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:26.610
Kanuka, do you read me?

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:30.660
I guess you heard. Take
command of Izumi in machine 1.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.450
Izumi, you're now under
Kanuka's command.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:35.580
Understand?

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:38.460
Roger.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:57.350
Attention, cornered criminal:
Can you hear me?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.060
The bath is completely surrounded.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:04.770
Release your hostage
and exit your Labor.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:09.450
Stay back,
or the old man goes squish!

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:13.910
Stop this. There's plenty
of other fish in the sea.

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:17.790
Shut up!
You don't understand!

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.620
She was the only one for me!

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.370
Yeah, everyone says that.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.840
They get dumped, and say,
"She's the only one for me."

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.340
"If I can't have her...

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.970
"I'll smash everything
and then kill myself."

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:38.470
"And then she'll be sorry."

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.940
But she won't be.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:46.900
A fool's death is buried
on page three of the paper.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:51.740
The woman laughs and
moves on to another man.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.360
Soon she's popping out the babies.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:58.620
She buys them bicycles, takes
them to school, and out shopping.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.790
And the world goes on.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.750
It's tragic, isn't it?

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.710
Well...

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.170
Let's put this behind us.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.340
You must be kidding!
You can't fool me!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:15.140
Either fight me, or go home!

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.680
Listen...

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.930
I won't listen!
Just go home!

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.560
Or else get me a date.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.520
The police don't do
that sort of thing.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:29.070
Then go home!
Scram, or the old man gets it!

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:38.580
Rescue complete!

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.410
Why you!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.840
Don't draw it out. Use your gun
and shoot his legs out.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.970
What are you doing?
Follow orders, Officer Izumi.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:03.680
I can handle it this way.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.610
Give up, or I'll use this!

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.570
That? I'm SO scared!

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.670
Now we're even!

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.510
I ordered you to shoot!

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:46.230
In that crowded neighborhood?
What if I missed?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.810
That's an excuse.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:54.190
You just didn't want to
shoot the LABOR!

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:58.200
Well the Labor didn't do anything!
His <i>pilot</i> was the criminal.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.120
You're too careless!

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.040
If you succeed, a surprise
move can take out an opponent.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.750
A show of force would
have ended things quickly.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:12.590
You aren't authorized to ignore
orders from the command car!

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:16.800
That's enough.
Let's stop here for today.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.090
But, Captain!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:23.810
Both of you write up reports.
They're due today, understand?

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:29.730
Under the circumstances,
a decision won't be easy.

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:36.280
Would Izumi have ignored the
same order from Shinohara?

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:38.700
This IS a tough one.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.410
I hadn't realized it,

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:46.120
but Division 2's main weakness
may be a lack of flexibility.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:49.410
You have some complex people
with strong opinions.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.830
That's one way to put it.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:57.050
It's the captain's job to
take problems like this,

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:01.590
and turn them into an
opportunity for growth.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.220
They need a delicate touch.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:20.570
Nautilus

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:23.780
Kanuka Clancy:
Born on Oahu, Hawaii.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.660
Top of her class at the
New York City police academy.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.290
Promoted to lieutenant last year.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.370
Noa Izumi: Born in
Tomakomai, Hokkaido.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:34.920
Had average marks at the
District Three police school,

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:38.090
but got special mention
in Labor piloting.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:43.260
Took detective training
and attended MIT.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.680
Received an MA in
electronics with top grades.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:50.890
Worked as a security guard
to pay for police school.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.650
Commended for excellent judgment,

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:58.400
but received three warnings
for arguing with her superiors.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:02.400
Superb athlete. Fourth
level judo, third level Aikido.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:05.620
Speaks German,
French, and Mandarin.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.870
Expert in marksmanship
and bomb disposal.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:13.750
Tried intramural basketball, but
washed out on her first match.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.130
Hobbies:
"I love Labors!"

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:20.670
Clancy beats her in everything.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:23.180
Sure, if we just go by the specs.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:28.140
But if they really understood
about each other...

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:31.060
they wouldn't have been
so bull-headed.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:40.110
A trial-and-error approach would
increase the pressure on Kanuka.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:46.490
It isn't as simple as the arguments
between Ota and Shinohara.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.830
Then what do you suggest?

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:54.080
The traditional approach
to this sort of problem.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:56.750
Isn't that a little simplistic?

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:02.050
It's the best way to get people
to open up to each other.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.350
But I'd like to ask one favor,
Shinobu.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:11.520
Can you loan me some?

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:14.980
Don't forget to pay me back!

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:22.440
Since this is the captain's treat,
I don't expect much.

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.990
Captain, what's going on here?

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:32.620
I thought it was time to thank you
for all your hard work.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:36.410
No thanks necessary.
It's our duty.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.920
Well, it doesn't matter,
just have fun.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:46.340
Speak freely and let your feelings out.
Eat, drink, and be merry!

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.930
I'll be back as soon as
I finish some business.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.110
So, how are you doing?

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:08.910
Captain, you're late.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.030
Where's Shinshi?

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:12.830
On the phone.

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:15.910
"Tamiko? It's Mikiyasu.
I'm so sorry!"

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:18.750
Sorry.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:22.590
- It must be hard, having a home.
- Well...

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.170
Serves you right for
getting married, stupid.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.430
I'll have some radish
and burdock root.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:34.100
So, Captain... what's up?
What's the occasion?

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:37.770
You guys work
so hard every day.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:40.600
It's our duty to work hard!

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.820
Well, no matter.
Let's enjoy ourselves.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.820
Shinohara having fun, sir!

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.610
More <i>sake</i>, miss,
and leave the bottle!

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.700
Chickwab, please.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:01.920
What's wrong?

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.250
Nothing. You really know
how to drink, don't you?

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:09.550
My family owns a bar. I used to
drink my father under the table.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:13.180
<i>Sake's</i> my poison.

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:14.050
Really?

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.810
Kanuka's no slouch, either.

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:23.480
Do you really need
to drink so fast?

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:26.820
Oh, we've barely started.
Bartender, one more!

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:27.820
Me too.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:29.570
What about you, sir?

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.700
Oh, I don't drink.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.530
A plate of wieners!

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:37.120
Steamed fishpaste.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:44.830
Once more!

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.380
Captain, Captain!

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:51.800
You should be drinking too!
Bring a glass!

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.470
I'm driving.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:57.180
One little drink won't hurt.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.890
Shinohara! Are you
inciting an officer to DUI?

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:07.230
Shut up! Go back to the dorm
and polish your bullets!

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.690
What was that?

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.200
Can't we drink quietly?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:18.240
Captain! I won't let anyone,
even you, break the law!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:19.410
I'm not drinking!

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:22.080
- Captain!
- What now?

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:27.960
Where's Noa? And Kanuka?
Why aren't they here?

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.260
Oh, they're over
on the far side.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.630
What a shame. Women shouldn't
drink alone. Let's call them over.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:40.470
Noa, Kanuka, even Nagumo!
I'll go get them.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.980
Don't you dare!
Women and wine don't mix.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:48.020
Yeah, looking at your face
gives them an instant hangover.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:51.780
Why, you!
And I was being nice!

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.780
Let's not talk about faces.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.030
Izumi, haven't you had enough?

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.660
I'm FINE!
This is NOTHING!

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:04.500
Have some <i>oden</i>.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:08.170
Straight <i>sake</i> is
bad for your stomach.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.050
You sound just like my mother!

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:16.680
Why are you having so much fun?

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.090
Kanuka?

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:22.640
What's wrong?
Aren't YOU having fun?

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:29.310
You're right!
We don't have enough <i>sake</i>!

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:31.570
Hey, one more!

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:41.160
You're always asking,
"Where's Noa? What's she doing?"

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:45.660
Your hovering keeps Izumi from
learning to be independent!

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:50.590
You should talk! You're the one
who's henpecked by Kanuka!

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.500
What?

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:57.260
You always say, "We don't
need women in the police."

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.090
But you're just a
trained monkey!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.350
Trained monkey?

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:05.930
Pandering to women and always
trying to show off! It's gross!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.600
Why, you!

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.230
What did you say?

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:14.480
I asked,
what did you just say?

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:15.940
Shinshi!

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:20.200
You're bachelors.
You don't know how hard life is!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.450
How can you be sarcastic
about having a home?

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.210
You don't have the right
to complain.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:28.000
We're sorry!

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:31.580
You think wine and
women don't mix?

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:38.510
Just what I expect from an idiot
who can't make a woman happy.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:40.300
Well, I...

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.390
Goto!

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.430
Excuse me.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:47.520
What's this?
Are you running away?

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:52.940
Of course not! I have to check up
on Izumi and the others!

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.900
You WERE running away!

00:18:56.230 --> 00:19:03.070
You sneak out
whenever there's trouble.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:06.740
You can't hold your liquor,
can you?

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:08.710
So what if I can't?

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.500
So what if I can't!

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:16.340
They're all against me.

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:21.720
Do you think I don't hear you
talking behind my back?

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:24.100
Miss, I'll have that drink after all.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:28.220
It's hard to have a home!

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:31.730
I love it, but it's so damn hard!

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:32.850
Here you go.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:33.520
Thanks.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:40.030
Tamiko!

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.990
He really CAN'T hold his liquor.
Is he your son?

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.160
MY son?

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.580
You still awake?

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.170
Yeah.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:56.710
I've wanted to ask you
for a while...

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:58.340
What?

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:02.220
You came to Japan all alone.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:09.310
Don't you miss anyone
back in America?

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:13.270
Grandma.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:15.810
Grandma.

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:21.440
Oh, your grandmother?

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.740
I wonder how she's
doing right now.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:30.620
I want to go home.
I want to go back home.

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:36.960
You're homesick?
So you ARE human after all.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.190
Is Yamazaki okay?

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.450
They're sound asleep.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.200
Good.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:24.050
There's an 808 in Kamiigusa.
Division 2, mobilize!

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:27.890
Are you okay?

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:31.140
Good morning!

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.270
Last night was great,
wasn't it, Kanuka?

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.600
You're feeling good?

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:40.320
Sure. I'm fine after
a night's sleep.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.230
We'll have to do that
again sometime!

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:47.820
A true bartender's daughter.
Noa wins the drinking contest.

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:53.410
Your entire team is hung over.
Was it worth it?

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.410
It works for my team.

00:21:56.870 --> 00:22:02.210
They're only beginning to learn
to trust each other.

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:04.880
It'll be hard.
They need a delicate touch.

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:09.590
The equipment's ready
except the pilots.

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:15.350
A drinking binge to
help your team bond?

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:18.690
Only you could make that work.

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:21.110
But there was one failure.

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:23.780
I never got a chance
to have a drink.

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:28.280
Why are we just talking?
We have to mobilize!

00:22:31.820 --> 00:22:35.660
Let's go face the day!

00:22:42.250 --> 00:22:45.460
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.590 --> 00:22:49.180
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:55.430
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:02.860 --> 00:23:04.940
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:07.860
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:12.450
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:17.120
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:19.960
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:24.130
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:30.630
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:35.890
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:38.430
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:41.640
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.730
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:51.900
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:57.950
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:04.580
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:09.710
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:09.710
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:17.140
In Tokyo Bay, inside the dike being
elected by the Babylon Project...

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:19.600
A humpback whale
comes wondering in.

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:21.640
The poor thing gets
weaker and weaker by the day.

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:23.350
Can't we do something?

00:24:23.390 --> 00:24:25.100
The Coast Guard,
the Fire Department,

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:28.690
and our own Division 2 are called in
to implement a rescue operation.

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:32.490
Oh, that's great!
But... gee, can we really pull it off?

00:24:32.700 --> 00:24:36.740
Next time, "A Whale That Sang a
Song." Target locked on!

00:24:36.120 --> 00:24:41.120
Next episode

00:24:36.120 --> 00:24:41.120
A Whale That Sang a Song
